/T (Flow Rack and Carton Flow)
/E (Flow Rack and Carton Flow)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
364 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 172 0 R
/T (Flow rack uses gravity-fed lanes that let product slide to the pick face as the front carton empties. It is the cheapest infrastructure upgrade in fulfillment. Compresses the pick face, keeps fast movers dense, reduces walk. For SKUs that move more than a few times a day, flow rack is almost always the right answer over standard shelving. The common mistake is slotting flow rack by what feels fast rather than by velocity data. Every 3PL at Stage 3 or above should be re-slotting at least monthly.)
/E (Flow rack uses gravity-fed lanes that let product slide to the pick face as the front carton empties. It is the cheapest infrastructure upgrade in fulfillment. Compresses the pick face, keeps fast movers dense, reduces walk. For SKUs that move more than a few times a day, flow rack is almost always the right answer over standard shelving. The common mistake is slotting flow rack by what feels fast rather than by velocity data. Every 3PL at Stage 3 or above should be re-slotting at least monthly.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
